<title>UK: EIB sets 14 billion yen dual currency bond.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 14 billion yen dual currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual currency bond was announced by joint lead managers LTCB International, CIBC Wood Gundy and Toyo Trust International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    14 BLN YEN    COUPON     5.46	MATURITY    24.MAR.00</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL-CURRENCY ISS/REOFF  100.0     PAY DATE    24.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.70	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (K) 500	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> NOTES	COUPON IN YEN, REDEMPTION IN A$</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
